# `bytes.slice(2, 6)` on a view out of a variable of the module was a closed read of "slice" and a call of an unknown callee, and what came back was anything: the loop behind it took 111 instructions an
# element. Link said that the variable's view stays as its class makes it; the table of receivers that stay as made listed no view at all, since the day a worker lengthened one under a loop
# (parallel/views-whose-memory-changes-while-a-loop-runs). That fault has its own door in the walk: a view says nothing where the program names what grows shared memory. So views are listed, and the
# receiver's door asks the same.
# The five other views are WRITTEN ON: an own method, another prototype, a constructor with a species, a name under a key that is put together, a hand-over to code nobody sees: none of them is listed.
# f2 = copyOfPart, f3 = placeOf, f4 = ownMethod, f5 = otherPrototype, f6 = species, f7 = nameByKey, f8 = ofHandedOut
# RUN: walk f2:Body f3:Body f4:Body f5:Body f6:Body f7:Body f8:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK-NOT: PropGet {{*}} key="slice"
# CHECK: Uint8Array @JSValue = CallBuiltin {{*}} overload=TypedArrayPrototypeSlice/0
# CHECK: GetTypedArrayLength
# CHECK-LABEL: code f3:Body
# CHECK-NOT: PropGet {{*}} key="indexOf"
# CHECK: overload=TypedArrayPrototypeIndexOf/0
# CHECK-LABEL: code f4:Body
# CHECK-NOT: overload=TypedArrayPrototypeSlice
# CHECK-LABEL: code f5:Body
# CHECK-NOT: overload=TypedArrayPrototypeSlice
# CHECK-LABEL: code f6:Body
# CHECK-NOT: overload=TypedArrayPrototypeSlice/0
# CHECK-LABEL: code f7:Body
# CHECK-NOT: overload=TypedArrayPrototypeSlice
# CHECK-LABEL: code f8:Body
# CHECK-NOT: overload=TypedArrayPrototypeSlice
# RUN(SHELL): run-in-shell globalThis.sink = value => { if (typeof value === "string") print(value); else value.slice = () => "handed out"; };
# SHELL: 42 | 3 | 0 | 0 | Uint8Array4 | 0 | 0 | 42 | 3 | own | of the other prototype | Uint16Array4 | under a key | handed out
